 ;; on its branch as the eval's :seon.eval/opened (seon.agent/untaken-facts)
 :seon.agent/opened [:set {:description "The ids of its evals that a reader of its page opened, kept on main."} :string]
 ;; main's head and its branch's merge base as it last heard them (seon.agent's state :main, :base), the commits the
 ;; page's branch views read, written by its turn, so a cold build draws what the live page does
 :seon.agent/main-commit [:uuid {:description "Main's head as the agent last heard it, the commit that its page's branch views read."}]
